## Summary

- expose `isReplySessionInitConflictError(error: unknown)` through
  `openclaw/plugin-sdk/error-runtime`;
- move the conflict error identity into a lightweight shared module;
- replace duplicated classification logic in Discord, Signal, Slack,
  Telegram, and WhatsApp;
- update the Plugin SDK API baseline, surface budget, and subpath docs.

## Behavior

The shared predicate recognizes:

- `ReplySessionInitConflictError` instances;
- strictly matched legacy conflict messages;
- raw legacy message strings;
- wrapped conflicts in `cause` and `error` chains;
- compatible error-like objects with an exact message.

It intentionally does not classify name-only or partial-message matches.

This normalizes wrapped-error handling and strict message matching across
channels. Retry counts, backoff, terminal behavior, and user-facing messages
are unchanged.

## Testing

- classifier tests: 25/25;
- Plugin SDK tests: 6/6;
- Discord: 138/138;
- Signal: 7/7;
- Slack: 13/13;
- WhatsApp: 54/54;
- Telegram added wrapped-conflict test passing;
- tsgo:core;
- check:test-types;
- plugin-sdk strict smoke;
- API check;
- surface check;
- deadcode checks;
- import-cycle checks;
- format/lint;
- git diff --check.

Four unrelated Windows-only failures were reproduced unchanged on the
upstream/main baseline: one SQLite EBUSY cleanup failure and three Telegram
path-separator assertions.

## Scope

- no retry or backoff changes;
- no terminal-notice changes;
- no new error code;
- no changes to PR #108899;
- QQBot migration is deferred until #108899 is merged.

## What Problem This Solves

Fixes an issue where editing a configured hook transform could leave the gateway running the old transform function after hooks hot reload rebuilt the mapping config.

## Why This Change Was Made

Hook mapping resolution now builds a candidate runtime snapshot without mutating the process-local transform cache. The transform cache generation is advanced only after the gateway accepts the new hooks runtime config at startup or after hot reload successfully resolves the candidate hooks config and reaches the runtime commit edge. A delayed import from an older generation can still finish its own delivery, but it no longer republishes into the current cache after an accepted reload, and a rejected candidate reload leaves the active transform cache untouched.

## User Impact

Operators can update hook transform files and have subsequent matching webhook deliveries use the edited transform without restarting the gateway.

## Evidence

- Production module boundary: `pnpm exec tsx ../../outputs/local-hook-transform-reload/proof-live.ts`

```text
$ pnpm exec tsx ../../outputs/local-hook-transform-reload/proof-live.ts
first-transform: before
after-rejected-candidate: before
after-reload: after
```

- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/gateway/hooks-mapping.test.ts`: 31 passed, including rejected-candidate and overlapping-import regressions.
- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/gateway/config-reload.test.ts`: 132 passed.
- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/gateway/server-reload-handlers.test.ts`: 98 passed, including invalid hooks reload preserving the active transform cache.
- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/gateway/server-runtime-config.test.ts`: 30 passed.
- `git diff --check`: passed.

<details>
<summary>proof-live.ts</summary>

```ts
import fs from "node:fs";
import os from "node:os";
import path from "node:path";
import { pathToFileURL } from "node:url";

const configDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), "openclaw-hook-transform-proof-"));
const transformsRoot = path.join(configDir, "hooks", "transforms");
fs.mkdirSync(transformsRoot, { recursive: true });
const transformPath = path.join(transformsRoot, "reloadable.mjs");

type HooksMappingModule = typeof import("./src/gateway/hooks-mapping.js");
let hooksMapping: HooksMappingModule;

function writeTransform(text: string) {
  fs.writeFileSync(
    transformPath,
    `export default () => ({ kind: "wake", text: ${JSON.stringify(text)} });\n`,
  );
}

function resolveCurrentMappings() {
  return hooksMapping.resolveHookMappings(
    {
      mappings: [
        {
          match: { path: "reloadable" },
          action: "agent",
          messageTemplate: "unused",
          transform: { module: "reloadable.mjs" },
        },
      ],
    },
    { configDir },
  );
}

function acceptMappings(mappings: ReturnType<typeof resolveCurrentMappings>) {
  hooksMapping.commitHookTransformMappingReload();
  return mappings;
}

async function runHook(mappings: ReturnType<typeof resolveCurrentMappings>) {
  const result = await hooksMapping.applyHookMappings(mappings, {
    payload: {},
    headers: {},
    url: new URL("http://127.0.0.1:18789/hooks/reloadable"),
    path: "reloadable",
  });
  if (!result?.ok || result.action?.kind !== "wake") {
    throw new Error(`unexpected hook result: ${JSON.stringify(result)}`);
  }
  return result.action.text;
}

async function main() {
  hooksMapping = await import(pathToFileURL(path.resolve("src/gateway/hooks-mapping.ts")).href);
  try {
    writeTransform("before");
    let mappings = acceptMappings(resolveCurrentMappings());
    console.log(`first-transform: ${await runHook(mappings)}`);
    writeTransform("after");
    resolveCurrentMappings(); // rejected candidate resolution must not invalidate the active cache
    console.log(`after-rejected-candidate: ${await runHook(mappings)}`);
    mappings = acceptMappings(resolveCurrentMappings());
    console.log(`after-reload: ${await runHook(mappings)}`);
  } finally {
    fs.rmSync(configDir, { recursive: true, force: true });
  }
}

void main();
```

</details>

